{"id": "20533598", "revid": "753665", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20533598", "title": "House Work (novel)", "text": "House Work is a novel by the American writer Kristina McGrath set in 1950s Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\nIt tells the story of a working-class family of five through shifting points of view. The novel's focus is on a mother's heroism in raising her three children alone after the disintegration of her marriage. Defying the advice of her parish priest, Anna Hallissey leaves her alcoholic husband and re-establishes a home for her children by cleaning other people's houses.\nThe novel was chosen by \"The New York Times Book Review\" as a notable book of the year in 1994."}
