{"id": "20534296", "revid": "14965160", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20534296", "title": "Henri Bacry", "text": "Henri Bacry (1928\u20132010) was Professor Emeritus at the Universit\u00e9 de la M\u00e9diterran\u00e9e. Henri Bacry was assistant of physics at the Facult\u00e9 des Sciences d'Alger and then Professor of mathematics at Lyc\u00e9e Bugeaud, before becoming, in 1969, Professor at the Facult\u00e9 des Sciences de Luminy. He was a visiting scholar at the Institute for Advanced Study in Princeton in 1966-6 and a researcher at CERN. He is the founder in 1972 of the International Colloquium of Group Theoretical Methods in Physics. He has numerous publications on theoretical physics, problems of symmetry in various fields ranging from relativity to particle physics, optics, physics of sound and statistical mechanics and some work in mathematics. "}
