{"id": "20535042", "revid": "7263350", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20535042", "title": "CaixaForum Madrid", "text": "CaixaForum Madrid is a cultural center in Madrid, Spain. Located in Paseo del Prado in a former power station, it is owned by the not-for-profit banking foundation \"la Caixa\". The art center opened its doors in 2008 and it hosts temporary art exhibitions and cultural events.\nThe cultural center was designed by the Swiss architects Herzog &amp; de Meuron and built by Ferrovial between 2001 and 2007. It was an old power station called Central Del Mediod\u00eda, from the 1900s. The \"Vertical Garden\" by Patrick Blanc at the square is also well-known."}
