{"id": "20535858", "revid": "43283345", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20535858", "title": "Theodas of Laodicea", "text": "Theudas of Laodicea (Greek: \u0398\u03b5\u03c5\u03b4\u03ac\u03c2 \u03cc \u039b\u03b1\u03bf\u03b4\u03b9\u03ba\u03b5\u03cd\u03c2) was a Pyrrhonist philosopher and physician of the Empiric school, in the 2nd century. He is mentioned by Diogenes La\u00ebrtius as being a native of Laodicea in Syria, a pupil of Antiochus of Laodicea, and a contemporary of Menodotus. A physician of this name is also quoted by Andromachus."}
